_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Description of the problem / feature request:\r\nGlobs of filegroups miss hidden (`.foo.bar`) files.\r\nI see this since I have an attribute in a rule that accepts certain file types (using `allow_files`), and when that attribute depends on the filegroup I get `in deps attribute of printer rule //attributes:some_target: '//attributes:sources' does not produce any printer deps files (expected .scala)`.  (In the above example the glob is for `*.scala` and there is a `.foo.scala` file).\r\nImportant to add that when the glob is on the attribute then it evaluates correctly (sees `.foo.scala`). When the glob is on the filegroup but the file is not hidden (`foo.scala`) it also works and finally when the filegroup has an explicit file (`srcs = [\".foo.scala\"]`) and the rule depends on the filegroup it also works. \r\n\r\nThe only case that doesn't work is attribute that depends on a filegroup that uses a glob that should evaluate to a single hidden file but does not.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Bugs: what's the simplest, easiest way to reproduce this bug? Please provide a minimal example if possible.\r\n\r\n```\r\ngit clone git@github.com:ittaiz/examples\r\ncd examples\r\ngit checkout patch-1\r\ncd rules/attributes\r\nbazel build :some_target #see failure\r\nll -a #see .foo.scala\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What operating system are you running Bazel on?\r\n\r\nmacOS 10.13.6\r\n\r\n### What's the output of `bazel info release`?\r\n\r\n1.1.0\r\n###  Have you found anything relevant by searching the web?\r\n\r\nI'm basically trying to work around #7516 by always making sure I have a file that matches the glob while not getting in the way of my users (hence why I want to hide the file) ","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4"